{
  "version": 1,
  "comment": "avatar converter, RigMap fixer: known third-party rigs and the supported avatar skeleton each maps onto. Matching strips an FBX namespace (everything up to the last ':' or '|') from every bone name, then the first of the profile's prefixes (case-insensitive regular expressions anchored at the start), and compares the rest with the keys of bones without regard to case. A profile is used when it names every bone the converter cannot insert (pelvis, head, and each side's upperarm, lowerarm, hand, thigh, calf and foot); the other required bones of the target (root, the spine, neck_01, the clavicles, ball) are inserted with no weights when the rig lacks them. Bones a profile maps whose hierarchy disagrees with the target skeleton's are left unmapped (optional bones) or refused (required ones). Weighted bones a profile does not map stay and fold into their nearest kept ancestor at upload; unweighted bones with nothing kept below them (Mixamo's *_End) are dropped. Add a rig by adding a profile here; a creator's guided mapping is saved in this format to <Project>/Saved/Mantle/RigProfiles.",
  "profiles": [
    {
      "id": "mixamo",
      "name": "Mixamo",
      "target": "ue4mannequin",
      "why": "Three spine bones (Spine, Spine1, Spine2) between Hips and the neck, the clavicles (LeftShoulder, RightShoulder) and the neck on the last of them, three-bone fingers and no twist bones: the UE4 Mannequin's layout bone for bone (spine_01 to spine_03, clavicle_l/r and neck_01 on spine_03). The UE5 Mannequin and MetaHuman hang the clavicles and neck on spine_05 of five spine bones, which Mixamo does not have. Mixamo has no root bone above Hips: root is inserted at the feet.",
