    {
      "id": "3dsmaxcat",
      "name": "3ds Max CAT",
      "target": "ue4mannequin",
      "why": "3ds Max's Character Animation Toolkit names each bone after its rig (\"Base Human\", \"Base-Human\" or the creator's own) with the side and part run on: Base-HumanPelvis, Base-HumanLUpperarm1. Spine1 to Spine3 then Ribcage, which carries the neck and the collarbones, so Ribcage is the UE4 Mannequin's spine_03 and Spine3 folds into spine_02. Limbs come in segments in a row (Upperarm1-3, Forearm1-3): the first of each is the bone and the others fold into it. Digit1x is the thumb (three joints); Digit2x to Digit5x are index to pinky with a metacarpal first (Digit21), which folds into the hand. Tails, belts and face bones fold into their nearest kept bone. No root bone above Pelvis: root is inserted at the feet.",
